---

import { orgPaths } from '../../../lib/tenant-paths';
export const getStaticPaths = orgPaths;

import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../../components/PageHead.astro';
import { activeOrg } from '../../../lib/tenant';

const org = activeOrg(Astro);

const stored = [
  ['Name', 'The name you choose to be published under, and the name you sign in with.'],
  ['Email address', 'To sign you in and to send you the messages listed below. Never shown publicly.'],
  ['School', 'What is shown on your published work. Marked unverified until a teacher confirms it.'],
  ['Graduation year', 'So the system knows when you have left, rather than guessing from silence.'],
  ['Teacher sponsor email', 'One message asking them to confirm your school. Nothing else, ever.'],
  ['Guardian name and email', 'One message asking permission, plus reminders if there is no answer.'],
  ['Your project work', 'Whatever you write into the system: notes, drafts, answers, links.'],
];

const notStored = [
  'Date of birth',
  'Home address',
  'Phone number',
  'Grades or test scores',
  'Race, ethnicity, or any demographic data',
  'Anything from your school records',
  'The contents of documents you link to',
];
---

<Base
  title="What we store"
  description="The complete list of what this service collects about a student, and what it does not."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="What we store"
    lede="The whole list is on this page. It is short because the shortest way to protect data is to never hold it."
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="note">
      <h4>Reading this site needs no account, and we store nothing about you</h4>
      <p>
        The published records, the guides, this season's programs, and the mistakes list
        need no account. Search runs in your browser against static files, so no search you
        type here is sent anywhere or logged by anyone.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:12px">
        One thing does leave your browser: the typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts, so
        Google receives the request and, with it, your IP address and browser. We would
        rather serve them ourselves and intend to. Until we do, saying so is better than
        a sentence that is nearly true.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>What an account stores</b><span>Seven things</span></div>
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {stored.map(([item, why]) => <tr><td><b>{item}</b></td><td>{why}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>What is never collected</b><span>Not optional, not stored</span></div>
      <ul class="prose">
        {notStored.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-top:14px">
        We do not read documents a student links to. We store the address and display where
        it points, and nothing fetches or opens it. We do not train models on student work,
        we do not sell data, we do not show advertising, and we do not build a profile of
        anyone for any purpose beyond running this service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>Permission</b><span>Before anything is published</span></div>
      <p class="prose">
        Accounts are for students aged 13 and over. At signup a student names a parent or
        guardian, who receives one message asking them to confirm. The student can work
        immediately and for fourteen days while that is outstanding, but
        <b>nothing is published before a guardian has confirmed</b>. After fourteen days
        without an answer the work is paused and kept safe; it returns the moment permission
        arrives. An account still unconfirmed after sixty days is deleted.
      </p>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-top:14px">
        A teacher sponsor separately confirms the school. Until they do, the affiliation
        shows as unverified on anything published.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>Who sees what</b><span>Inside the system</span></div>
      <ul class="prose">
        <li>Your project work: you, your co-authors, any mentor assigned to it, and the officers and advisor who run the program.</li>
        <li>Your email address: officers and the advisor. It is never rendered on a public page, in any form.</li>
        <li>Feedback from a mentor: attached to the project and visible to officers and the advisor. There is no private messaging between an adult and a student here.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>Deleting your account</b><span>Always available</span></div>
      <p class="prose">
        From your settings, at any time, without giving a reason. You are shown what
        will go, warned that it cannot be undone, and asked to type a confirmation.
        After that the account, your notebook entries wherever they are, your projects,
        the files behind them and any record published only by you are removed from our
        active systems. They cannot be recovered.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        <b>Deleting your account never deletes somebody else's work.</b> A project you
        share with another author needs every author to agree before it goes; if they do
        not, you come off it and the project stays with them. Guidance you wrote for a
        whole program, and reviews of other people's manuscripts, need the program's
        teacher to agree for the same reason. Where nothing is shared, nothing is asked
        and the deletion is immediate.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="note warn" style="margin-top:28px">
      <h4>This page describes how the software is built. The full legal policy is in review.</h4>
      <p>
        The privacy policy and terms of service are with counsel and will be published here
        before any student outside a pilot uses the working surface. If something on this
        page and something in those documents ever disagree, tell {org.name} and we will fix
        the discrepancy rather than argue it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
